body:
The field comment says PluginInstallToken is for requests to the Grafana.com /plugins API, but the PR also uses it for other plugin-related endpoints (e.g., /api/gnet/* proxy and plugin downloads). Consider broadening the comment to avoid misleading future readers about the token’s scope.



        Suggested change






            	// PluginInstallToken is the auth token for requests to the Grafana.com /plugins API.



            	// PluginInstallToken is the auth token for Grafana.com plugin-related requests,



            	// including plugin API calls, downloads, and related proxy endpoints.

Adding PluginInstallToken() to the CommandLine interface requires updating all existing utils.CommandLine implementations (including test fakes). For example, pkg/cmd/grafana-cli/commands/upgrade_command_test.go defines baseCommandLine/testCommandLine that currently don’t implement PluginInstallToken(), which will cause the grafana-cli test package to fail to compile. Please add a default implementation there (and anywhere else implementing CommandLine) or provide a backward-compatible adapter.



        Suggested change






            	GcomToken() string



            	PluginInstallToken() string



            }



            	GcomToken() string



            }







            type PluginInstallTokenProvider interface {



            	PluginInstallToken() string



            }







            func GetPluginInstallToken(c CommandLine) string {



            	if provider, ok := c.(PluginInstallTokenProvider); ok {



            		return provider.PluginInstallToken()



            	}







            	return ""



            }
